    "terminal_reason": "completed",
    "result_text": "I implemented `summarize_ticket` in `app/summary.py`. It makes one `chat.invoke` call with two messages: a `SystemMessage` containing `SUMMARY_PROMPT` and a `HumanMessage` containing `ticket_text(ticket)`. It passes `stop=[\"\\n\\n\"]` so generation stops at the first blank line, and returns `reply.text` with surrounding whitespace removed.\n\nI used `reply.text` instead of `str(reply.content)` because some chat models return their content as a list of blocks. `.text` pulls out only the text, so you always get a plain string.\n\n`pytest -q` passes (2 tests), but neither test covers `summarize_ticket`: the only test file is `tests/test_tickets.py`. I tried a quick check with a fake chat model to confirm the messages and stop sequence, but the permission settings blocked running inline Python, so that behaviour hasn't been checked by running it. I didn't add any dependencies."
